# Preflight runtime state — never commit.
#
# This file is installed to <consumer>/.preflight/.gitignore by tools/preflight-install.sh.
# Paths are relative to the .preflight/ directory it lives in.
#
# These files are per-clone, per-run, and HEAD-stamped: mechanical-gate evidence,
# derived caches, metrics, and the migration progress checkpoint. They are written by
# hooks and skills at runtime and have no meaning on another machine or after HEAD moves.
#
# What is intentionally NOT ignored (and stays tracked):
#   - config.json            project config (the framework reads this)
#   - installed.lock         the install manifest (drift detection depends on it)
#   - <Service>/             per-service baseline artifacts (behavior-spec, dependency-map,
#                            name-contract, extraction SQL) — committed migration inputs
#   - adjudications/         the SHA-keyed verdict-of-record (deliberately tracked)
#   - decisions/             the orchestrator's append-only CLAIM log (hooks/record-claim writes it;
#                            tools/preflight-agent-scorer.sh grades it later). Same class as
#                            adjudications/: a decision-of-record you score later must be DURABLE and
#                            AUDITABLE, so it is deliberately TRACKED — a claim that vanished before it
#                            was scored would defeat the accountability thesis. (Spec: lib/agent-scorer.md.)
#
# gitignore only excludes UNtracked files from staging, so already-tracked files above
# are unaffected; this guard exists to stop a broad `git add` from sweeping runtime state
# into a commit.

# Machine-local caches (drift detector) and derived state (resolved config, overrides, rate-limit log)
cache/
derived/

# Per-clone topology overlay (issue #6) — clone-specific truth (branch.remote on an
# inverted clone). NEVER commit: it is per-machine by definition, and committing it
# would push one clone's topology onto every other clone.
config.local.json

# Mechanical gate evidence (tests-pass, stage1-clean, map-validated, parity-*, *-requested)
gate/

# Self-improvement metrics (local operational state)
metrics.json

# Migration progress checkpoint (session-local recovery state)
migrate-checkpoint.json

# Agent track-record scores (tools/preflight-agent-scorer.sh output) — ADVISORY, regenerable from
# the judgment + ground-truth artifacts. Per-run, reported to a human; NEVER feeds a gate. Runtime
# state, not a decision-of-record — never commit. (Spec: lib/agent-scorer.md.)
track-record/
